  "trigger": "User requested one last iteration to make sure the pagination design plan missed nothing.",
  "requirements": [
    "Recheck the complete public, runtime, documentation, package and proof adoption surface rather than trust the prior final plan.",
    "Reject any surface-local paint design that wakes every mounted text node; preserve keyed semantic paint, native text flow and per-surface isolation.",
    "Make fragmentation explicit and invalid-state-resistant while preserving text, atomic media and exact direct-child table jobs with inferred callbacks.",
    "Leave a complete executable plan with honest design evidence, production gates and a fresh ledger record without changing product source."
  ],
  "evidenceReuse": "Reuses the seven-unit pagination audit, the prior Task plan, current 58-test pagination partition and unchanged derivation/lifetime/geometry receipts. Re-read the current decoration store, EditableText/EditableTextFlow, pagination, example, package and documentation owners. Replaced the false-positive paint probe, strengthened provider lowering/type proof, added a per-document font-owner probe, and reran all six design probes, package tests, TypeScript and relative links.",
  "summary": "Final pagination plan: PagedEditable owns live layout, projection, exact-ref reads and one private keyed surface-composite decoration store; measurePages remains the one-shot headless job. Fragmentation is text, atomic owner or exact direct children, with source paths derived internally. Generic geometry/path lookup, caller unit paths, page-break authority, the live controller and box/split protocols are cut. The full Plate/Plite docs, generated registry and release-check adoption surface is now explicit.",
  "verdict": "pursue",
  "previous": "2026-09-15-pagination-design-plan",
  "relation": "supersedes",
  "alternatives": [
    "Rejected the prior raw map-valued paint context: stable slice references did not prevent every context consumer from rendering. One private surface-composite PliteDecorationStore preserves the existing keyed path and wakes only changed node keys.",
    "Rejected text plus caller-authored unit paths: it permitted duplicate, foreign, missing and reordered partitions. Text, atomic and direct-children encode the only current relationships and derive source paths internally.",
    "Cut public getPageLayoutGeometry and getPageLayoutFragments: no independent production caller exists; page arrangement belongs to PagedEditable and raw fragment facts already exist in PageLayoutSnapshot.",
    "Retained PageLayoutEngine, built-in estimated/Pretext factories, page settings codec and one-shot measurePages because custom/headless measurement remains an independent current job.",
    "Rejected claims of automatic renderer-DOM measurement, exact glyph/export fidelity, repeated headers, row continuations or image slicing. Those capabilities lack an implemented owner and native proof."
  ],
  "proofLimits": "Planning only: seven expected feature dispositions addressed, no product source or existing tests edited. Six disposable design probes pass 298 assertions; the current pagination partition passes 58 tests/213 assertions/four files; the TypeScript 7.0.2 proposed-signature/import program passes with a stable Plite source fingerprint; 62 relative links resolve. The paint and font-owner probes use happy-dom or mocks, packing uses premeasured inputs, and the type sketch declares proposed signatures. No production candidate, native browser/device/IME, real FontFaceSet/glyph, custom renderer DOM measurement, accessibility/print, packed release or end-to-end settled-layout claim.",
